I can understand your concern.  While a regular doctor can provide some initial relief, a toothache is typically a dental issue. I would recommend visiting an emergency dentist or your regular dentist as soon as possible. They can assess the situation and provide the correct treatment. In the meantime, you can try taking:
- Over-the-counter pain relievers like ibuprofen or acetaminophen;
- Applying a cold compress to Ice the area;
- Avoiding hot or cold foods and drinks;
- Rinsing your mouth with warm salt water.

